  "description": "This dataset comprises 64-channel EEG recordings from 62 participants (31 pairs) engaged in a computerized Rock-Paper-Scissors game consisting of 480 competitive trials. The study investigates neural mechanisms underlying competitive decision-making through multivariate decoding approaches, providing insights into brain activity patterns during strategic social interactions.",
  "methods_description": "EEG data were recorded from 62 participants organized into 31 pairs during a computerized Rock-Paper-Scissors game lasting approximately 1 hour, with 480 games played per session using 64-channel electrode montage.",
